      "text": "```\n  EGYPTIAN BLUE (calcium copper silicate, CaCuSi₂O₅):\n    Earliest synthetic pigment (~3000 BCE)\n    Manufactured: quartz + copper + calcium + natron → kiln firing\n    Blue color; used on tomb paintings, funerary objects\n    Fluorescent in near-IR — can be detected and imaged today"
